From 58b2737a1fb09e8c5282eb43ded7c3688be500c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:07:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0310-port-madvise-hardware-page.patch

port: madvise() on a 4 KiB-page kernel with 16 KiB user maps. xnu-11417's
madvise_sanitize() aligns the range to the user map's page (16 KiB) before
mach_vm_behavior_set(); xnu-8796 passed the raw range, which
mach_vm_behavior_set() aligns to the hardware page for the reuse
behaviors. libmalloc releases 4 KiB pages with MADV_FREE_REUSABLE (it uses
the kernel page size), so 11417 discarded the 12 KiB of live heap next to
each one: launchd died in _libSystem_initializer (free_list_checksum_botch,
an XPC object with isa 0, dictionary nodes reading 0xff..) under iOS 16 and
iPadOS 18 alike. Found with the sweettrace syscall log: the corrupted node
(0x101205f90) and the madvise (0x101207000, 0x1000) shared one 16 KiB page.
The generic boards now align madvise to PAGE_MASK.
---
 bsd/kern/kern_mman.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_mman.c b/bsd/kern/kern_mman.c
index d3d99936..3c682a78 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_mman.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_mman.c
@@ -1379,8 +1379,22 @@ madvise_sanitize(
 	addr_u = vm_sanitize_canonicalize_ut_addr(user_map, addr_u);
 #endif /* HAS_MTE || HAS_MTE_EMULATION_SHIMS */
 
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) || defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_A5XELTE)
+	/*
+	 * sweet: 4 KiB-page kernel, 16 KiB user maps. Aligning to the map's page
+	 * here widened libmalloc's 4 KiB MADV_FREE_REUSABLE to the whole 16 KiB
+	 * page and discarded 12 KiB of live heap: launchd died in libSystem
+	 * start-up (free-list checksum, zeroed isa) under iOS 16 and iPadOS 18.
+	 * Align to the hardware page, as xnu-8796's madvise did by passing the
+	 * range through; mach_vm_behavior_set() still picks the map page for the
+	 * behaviors that need it.
+	 */
+	return vm_sanitize_addr_size(addr_u, len_u, VM_SANITIZE_CALLER_MADVISE,
+	           PAGE_MASK, user_map, VM_SANITIZE_FLAGS_SIZE_ZERO_FALLTHROUGH, start, end, size);
+#else
 	return vm_sanitize_addr_size(addr_u, len_u, VM_SANITIZE_CALLER_MADVISE,
 	           user_map, VM_SANITIZE_FLAGS_SIZE_ZERO_FALLTHROUGH, start, end, size);
+#endif
 }
 
 int
